      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=3{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}-5t.$ Calculate the acceleration $a$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}-5t) \\\\  & =9{t}^{2}+12t-5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
